PART 2: ARK ADDITIONAL TERMS
=============================================================================

These terms add conditions to every license you get under Part 1. Words
defined in Part 1 (software, licensor, you, your company, use) mean the same
here. The licensor is visiuun. A "derived work" is any work based on the
software, including modified versions, forks, ports, partial copies, and
apps built from its code.

2.1  Credit is mandatory.
     If you distribute the software or a derived work, or make either
     available to anyone else in any form (source code, compiled app,
     installer, app store listing, website or service), you must:

     (a) keep every copyright notice, every "Required Notice:" line, and
         this entire file, unchanged, with every copy;

     (b) show this credit line, readable and unabbreviated:

             Based on Ark by visiuun: https://github.com/visiuun/ark-browser

         both (i) inside the app, on its About, Settings or credits screen,
         where a user can find it without special effort, and (ii) on every
         page where you offer it, such as your README, release page,
         website or store listing;

     (c) state clearly, in the same places, that you changed the software,
         if you did.

     You may not remove, hide, shorten, obscure or bury the credit, for
     example by making it unreadable, putting it somewhere users would not
     reasonably look, or showing it only to some users.

2.2  No passing off.
     A derived work you distribute must have a name and an icon that are
     clearly different from "Ark", "Ark Browser" and the Ark logo, and must
     not suggest that visiuun made, endorses, supports or is responsible for
     it. Saying truthfully that it is based on Ark is allowed, and required
     by 2.1.

2.3  What counts as commercial.
     In addition to everything Part 1 does not permit, the following are
     commercial purposes. They are not permitted under these terms, no
     matter who does them (individuals and noncommercial organizations
     included), and need a separate written license from visiuun:

     (a) selling the software or a derived work, or charging any fee for
         downloading, installing, accessing, unlocking, supporting or
         updating it;
     (b) putting advertising, sponsored or affiliate content, paid search
         placement, referral codes, or any other paid promotion in it;
     (c) collecting, selling, sharing or otherwise monetizing data about
         the people who use it;
     (d) preinstalling, bundling or shipping it with, or as part of, any
         product or service that is sold or that earns money for anyone,
         or using it inside a for-profit company's product or service;
     (e) being paid, in money or anything else of value, to distribute it
         or a derived work;
     (f) using its source code to train, fine-tune or evaluate a machine
         learning model that is offered commercially.

     Asking for voluntary donations for your own free, noncommercial fork
     is allowed, as long as nothing in it is locked, limited or changed for
     people who do not donate.

2.4  Same terms for everyone downstream.
     Everyone who receives the software or a derived work from you gets it
     under these same terms (Parts 1 and 2), and you may not offer it under
     terms that drop or weaken any of them. Code you wrote yourself that
     stands on its own is yours to license as you like, but any copy that
     combines it with the software stays under these terms.

2.5  Extra permission: using Ark as a browser.
     Anyone, including people at work and organizations of any kind, may
     install and use the software, unmodified or modified only for their own
     use, as their web browser for any purpose. This permission covers
     browsing only; it does not allow anything listed in 2.3.

2.6  Contributions.
     If you submit a contribution (code, text, images or other material) to
     this repository, you keep your copyright and will be credited, and you
     grant visiuun a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free license to use,
     modify and distribute your contribution under these terms or any other
     terms, including commercial ones. Only submit work you have the right
     to submit.

2.7  Commercial licenses.
     To do something these terms don't allow, ask visiuun through
     https://github.com/visiuun. Nothing beyond these terms is permitted
     unless agreed in writing.

2.8  Violations.
     Breaking any term in Part 2 is breaking these terms under Part 1,
     including its Violations and Termination sections, so the 32-day
     chance to fix a first, notified violation applies here too.

